📖 Project Overview
This repository showcases a comprehensive GIS project using open-source tools to manage, publish, and visualize spatial data effectively. The project leverages a stack of GIS tools, including Apache Tomcat, GeoServer, MapStore, QGIS, and Geocat Bridge, to build a workflow for spatial data analysis and interactive web mapping.

🚀 Project Features
Apache Tomcat Configuration
Set up and configured Apache Tomcat as a hosting environment for GeoServer.
GeoServer for Spatial Data Publishing
Published geospatial data in OGC-compliant formats such as WMS, WFS, and WCS.
QGIS for Spatial Data Preparation
Preprocessed, analyzed, and styled spatial datasets using QGIS.
Geocat Bridge Integration
Seamlessly published QGIS-styled layers to GeoServer using Geocat Bridge.
MapStore for Web-Based Mapping
Created interactive dashboards to visualize and interact with spatial layers.
Dashboards and Query Functionalities
Built dashboards with multiple layers, filter options, and spatial query functionalities.

