🛠️ Tools and Technologies Used
Apache Tomcat: Web server for hosting GeoServer.
GeoServer: OGC-compliant geospatial data server.
QGIS: Desktop GIS tool for spatial data processing and styling.
Geocat Bridge: QGIS plugin for data publishing.
MapStore: Web-based mapping and dashboard creation tool.

📋 Requirements
To replicate this project, you will need:
Apache Tomcat 9.x or later
GeoServer 2.x or later
QGIS 3.x
Geocat Bridge plugin for QGIS
MapStore

🛠️ Setup Guide
Install Apache Tomcat and GeoServer
Follow the instructions in Scripts/installation_guide.md to install and configure Apache Tomcat and GeoServer.

Prepare and Style Data in QGIS
Use QGIS to preprocess and style geospatial datasets. Save the project files and styles in the QGIS/ directory.

Publish Layers Using Geocat Bridge
Install the Geocat Bridge plugin in QGIS and follow the steps in Scripts/publish_layers.md to publish your layers to GeoServer.

Create Dashboards in MapStore
Configure MapStore to visualize your layers. Use the provided MapStore-Dashboards/ JSON files as templates or create your own.


